<title>INDIA: Indian soybean prices end lower on new arrivals.</title>
<headline>Indian soybean prices end lower on new arrivals.</headline>
<dateline>INDORE, India 1996-09-19</dateline>
<text>
<p>Indian soybean prices fell sharply on Thursday on increased new season arrivals from central India markets, dealers said.</p>
<p>Prices fell by 500-600 rupees per tonne in central India while they eased by 600-700 rupees in plant delivery conditions.</p>
<p>Dealers said new arrivals from western Maharashtra state were quoted at 12,300-12,500 rupees per tonne.</p>
<p>Soyoil prices were down on increased selling against poor demand. Soyoil solvent was down by 500 rupees and soyoil refined was down by 300 rupees.</p>
<p>Soymeal prices were steady but rapeseed extraction prices firmed on good export demand. Soymeal yellow was $300-302 per tonne for September-October shipment in current season, and $280-282 for November, December and January shipments. Rapeseed extraction was $134 per tonne in export. Rapeseed extraction was 4,600 rupees FOR (Free on Rail) Bedibunder and was 4,550-4,575 rupees FOR (Free on Rail) Bhavnagar.</p>
